/target
# The vendored vt100 fork carries its own in-module tests, run with
# `cargo test --manifest-path vendor/vt100/Cargo.toml`; that generates a
# second lockfile and target dir which are build artifacts, not source.
/vendor/vt100/Cargo.lock
/vendor/vt100/target

# Agent worktrees: `isolation: "worktree"` gives a subagent its own checkout
# under here so it can build and write scratch harnesses without touching the
# main tree. They are whole repo copies and pure scratch — auto-removed when
# the agent finishes. `.claude/` itself stays tracked (agents/, settings).
/.claude/worktrees/

# graphify (the knowledge-graph tool wired up in `.opencode/`): its *outputs*
# are committed on purpose — `graph.json`, `graph.html`, `GRAPH_REPORT.md`,
# `manifest.json` and the curated `.graphify_labels.json` are the artifact the
# repo wants to keep and diff. What it writes *beside* them is not:
#   - `cost.json` is one machine's token-spend ledger, appended to every run.
#   - `cache/` is ~130 content-hash blobs (4.5 MB and growing per rebuild) —
#     re-derivable from the tree, so it costs history weight and buys nothing.
#   - `.graphify_python` / `.graphify_root` hold **absolute paths on whoever
#     ran it** (a home directory and a checkout location), so they are wrong
#     for every other clone by construction.
/graphify-out/cost.json
/graphify-out/cache/
/graphify-out/.graphify_python
/graphify-out/.graphify_root
